19:T7d9,<p>A gravity-powered descent cart carries no motor. Descent grade supplies the motion; the chassis, the brake and the terrain interface do the rest of the engineering work. That is the brief the GC-SPORT-01 is built to — a certified, all-season chassis engineered for two terrain configurations, not a seasonal toy built for one.</p>
<h2>The wheel-to-ski conversion</h2>
<p>The GC-SPORT-01 chassis mounts the terrain interface at the same certified attachment points regardless of season. For pavement, gravel and hardpack, that interface is the standard wheel assembly. For packed snow, it is the Ski Assembly Kit (GC-SKI-200): a certified ski conversion with a tool-free binding, 780mm ski length, rated to a 25% descent grade. Swapping between the two is a binding release and re-engage on the same chassis — no separate frame, no second vehicle to maintain, no re-certification per season.</p>
<h2>The certified chassis</h2>
<p>The GC-SPORT-01 is the flagship convertible chassis: certified wheel and ski assemblies included, rated to a 120kg load across both configurations. A chassis that is only certified in one mode is not a seasonal vehicle — it is a wheeled vehicle with an aftermarket ski attached. The GC-SPORT-01&#39;s rated load and certification hold across the conversion, which is what makes the swap a configuration change rather than a downgrade.</p>
<h2>The Shimano dual-disc brake</h2>
<p>Stopping is the one job on a gravity-powered vehicle that cannot be approximate. The Shimano Dual Brake Kit (GC-BRK-180) is a hydraulic dual-disc set, 180mm rotors front and rear, tested against the ECE R100 braking standard. It ships as the braking system for the GC-SPORT-01 chassis in both wheel and ski configuration — the same rotor size and test standard whichever terrain interface is mounted.</p>
<p>You can see the conversion itself, not just read the spec sheet, in the <a href="/#bay">chassis conversion demonstration</a> on our homepage.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
